{"name":"Yellow Mana","hex":"#fdfcbf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"mana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Power, prestige; specifically, a form of supernatural energy in Polynesian religion that inheres in things or people. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Magical energy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of mina (“ancient unit of weight or currency”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mana (series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mana series, known in Japan as Seiken Densetsu , is an action role-playing game series created by Koichi Ishii, with development formerly from Square, and is currently owned by Square Enix. The series began in 1991 as Final Fantasy Adventure, a Game Boy handheld side story to Square's flagship franchise Final Fantasy. The Final Fantasy elements were subsequently dropped starting with the second installment, Secret of Mana, in order to become its own series. It has grown to include games of various genres within the fictional world of Mana, with recurring stories involving a world tree, its associated holy sword, and the fight against forces that would steal their power. Several character designs, creatures, and musical themes reappear frequently."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(series)"},{"title":"Mana (electorate)","blocks":[{"text":"Mana is a New Zealand electorate, returning a single member to the New Zealand House of Representatives. The current MP for Mana is Barbara Edmonds of the Labour Party. She has held this position since the 2020 general election."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Mana_electorate%2C_2014.svg/330px-Mana_electorate%2C_2014.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(electorate)"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mana series' Ring Command menu (from Trials of Mana)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARingmenu.png"},{"srcset"